    {
      "short_id": "short264",
      "angle": "The seven-hundred-thousand-dollar award separated the decedent's account from the survivors' pain and grief, then survived a waived challenge.",
      "avoids": "No causal claim that waiting caused death; no depiction of the patient; no claim that EMTALA guarantees good treatment.",
      "funnel_question_left_for_longform": "What argument did the appeals court refuse to reach because the hospital raised it too late?",
      "loop": true,
      "loop_join": "The last line returns to the two-part award introduced at the start.",
      "era": "Puerto Rico, 1991",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "L1",
          "text": "The jury awarded seven hundred thousand dollars, but the opinion divided that number into two different accounts with different recipients and different injuries.",
          "delivery": "intense",
          "source_lines": [
            "Seven hundred thousand dollars in total."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L2",
          "text": "Two hundred thousand dollars was assessed on the decedent's account and made payable to the heirs, tied to her own hours of suffering.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Then the money."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L3",
          "text": "Five hundred thousand dollars addressed the survivors' pain, suffering, and mental anguish: three children and four grandchildren named by category.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "And five hundred thousand dollars for the pain, suffering, and mental anguish experienced by the survivors — one hundred thousand apiece for the three children, and fifty thousand apiece for the four grandchildren."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L4",
          "text": "The evidence described her as the family hub, and one witness called her the trunk of the family tree.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "It is hard to doubt, the opinion says, that the plaintiffs suffered when the woman described by one witness as the trunk of the family tree was cut down."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L5",
          "text": "The hospital challenged the damages after trial, but it had not preserved the legal theory in the required pretrial order or directed-verdict motion.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "This was a waiver, pure and simple."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L6",
          "text": "The panel called that move locking the barn door long after the horse had bolted: the argument arrived after the procedural chance to make it.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "This motion is a classic example of a litigant locking the barn door long after the horse has bolted."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L7",
          "text": "The court ordered no remittitur, reversed nothing, and left the jury's assessment intact without deciding every broader question the case raised.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Nothing was reversed. Nothing was vacated. No remittitur was ordered."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L8",
          "text": "The total therefore returns to its two parts: her account for the wait, and the family's separate suffering after losing its center.",
          "delivery": "calm",
          "source_lines": [
            "Seven hundred thousand dollars in total."
          ],
          "claims": []
        }
      ],
